# A THIRD CELL THAT NOBODY WALKS INTO.
#
# It sits diagonally from seam_a at (1,1) and orthogonally from seam_b, so it is
# within a radius of 1 of BOTH: an observer in either holds it, and walking from
# one to the other must not make the server send it again.
#
# That is the whole reason it exists. With only two cells every crossing swaps
# self and neighbour, nothing is retained, and "a held neighbour is re-stated
# rather than re-sent" has nothing to be true of. See server/edge/test/seam.test.js.
#
# No stub and no seam: it is never entered and never walked out of.
body radius 0.3333 height 1.1667

sector floor 0 ceil 8 floortex FLOOR1 ceiltex CEIL1
  vertex 10 10 wall tex WALL1
  vertex 30 10 wall tex WALL1
  vertex 30 30 wall tex WALL1
  vertex 10 30 wall tex WALL1
end

spawn start 20 20 1
